concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56bv a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56BV Commission may intervene if fee for disclosing or using"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56bv ;
    values:originalText "chargeable CDR data is unreasonable etc. Intervening for a class of CDR participants (1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, determine: (a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount of a fee, that a specified class of CDR participants for specified chargeable CDR data may charge (or cause to be charged) for either or both of the following matters (the chargeable matters): (i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances because of a requirement under the consumer data rules to do so; (ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and (b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee; if the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participants would otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable having regard to the criteria in subsection (4). Intervening for a particular CDR participant (2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a CDR participant for specified chargeable CDR data, determine: (a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount of a fee, that the CDR participant may charge (or cause to be charged) for either or both of the following matters (the chargeable matters): (i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances because of a requirement under the consumer data rules to do so; (ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and (b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee; if the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participant would otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable having regard to the criteria in subsection (4). Note: The determination is reviewable (see Subdivision F).  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "chargeable CDR data is unreasonable etc. Intervening for a class of CDR participants (1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, determine: (a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount of a fee, that a specified class of CDR participants for specified chargeable CDR data may charge (or cause to be charged) for either or both of the following matters (the chargeable matters): (i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances because of a requirement under the consumer data rules to do so; (ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and (b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee; if the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participants would otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable having regard to the criteria in subsection (4). Intervening for a particular CDR participant (2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a CDR participant for specified chargeable CDR data, determine: (a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount of a fee, that the CDR participant may charge (or cause to be charged) for either or both of the following matters (the chargeable matters): (i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances because of a requirement under the consumer data rules to do so; (ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and (b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee; if the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participant would otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable having regard to the criteria in subsection (4). Note: The determination is reviewable (see Subdivision F).  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "791a643df153c7bd4e28e1f0dfed8f7d5ad693fac5c43e6b1a2823ded1f2542d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56bv-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024-sch-1-sec-56bv-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf> ;
    dc:source "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2024.pdf, p.31" .
doc:sch-1-sec-56bv a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56BV Commission may intervene if fee for disclosing or using" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "chargeable CDR data is unreasonable etc. Intervening for a class of CDR participants (1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, determine: (a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount of a fee, that a specified class of CDR participants for specified chargeable CDR data may charge (or cause to be charged) for either or both of the following matters (the chargeable matters): (i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances because of a requirement under the consumer data rules to do so; (ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and (b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee; if the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participants would otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable having regard to the criteria in subsection (4). Intervening for a particular CDR participant (2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a CDR participant for specified chargeable CDR data, determine: (a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount of a fee, that the CDR participant may charge (or cause to be charged) for either or both of the following matters (the chargeable matters): (i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances because of a requirement under the consumer data rules to do so; (ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable circumstances as the result of such a disclosure; and (b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee; if the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participant would otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable having regard to the criteria in subsection (4). Note: The determination is reviewable (see Subdivision F).  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer .

